{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>Speak… and you shall say… any man….</b> He repeated <b>speak and you shall say</b>, and also changed the expression, and also repeated <b>any man, any man</b>, because there are two gradations in suspected wives: one is pure and one is defiled. The defiled one — her belly will swell and her thigh will fall, etc., while the pure one is praised and will be sown with seed. Therefore He said <b>speak</b> and <b>say</b> — <b>speak</b> for the defiled one, and a soft <b>say</b> for the pure one whose husband is jealous for her, for HaShem will sustain her heart through the assurances stated [in the verse] if the woman has not been defiled. And for this same reason He repeated saying <b>any man, any man</b>, and it is along the lines of what they said, their memory for blessing (Megillah 12b), in saying ״ומעלה בו מעל״ — if she committed treachery against him, he too is [implicated], etc. And from now on a person might say: if he was jealous of his wife and he knows himself that there is no treachery in him, her examination should be up to him through his own actions in place of the drinking [of the bitter waters], and he would hold her in purity even after warning and seclusion. Therefore it says <b>any man, any man</b> — whether one who knows himself that he is a pure man, or one who is not pure, he must bring her to the priest." "<b>Or perhaps</b> it was to this that the verse intended with the doubling <b>speak and you shall say</b>: both for one who thinks not to bring her, on the grounds that he knows himself that he is pure, and also so as not to impair her presumed status; and His saying <b>and you shall say</b> is a soft saying for one who desires the matter. Or, for each and every person there is both a hard <b>speak</b> and a soft <b>say</b>: for one in whom there is treachery, although he has a hard <b>speak</b> because his wickedness will be revealed in public, nevertheless there is a benefit for him in distancing himself from stumbling, so that he not continue lying with a defiled woman. And for one who is pure, he has a hard <b>speak</b> to compel him to subject his wife [to the ordeal], and he has a <b>say</b> that sustains the heart — that the woman will be cleared and sown with seed, etc.:"], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:06:20.931067077Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}